   "validatorId": "y11ty-do-now",
   "validatorKey": "y11ty_do_now",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Variables and Constants (1 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is a score a variable?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It changes while the game runs.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">From last lesson. Write <strong>variable</strong> or <strong>constant</strong>.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ty-do-now-a\">(a) The number of seconds in a minute: 60 [1]</label><input id=\"y11ty-do-now-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Variables and Constants (1 of 2) part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ty-do-now-b\">(b) A player's score in a game [1]</label><input id=\"y11ty-do-now-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Variables and Constants (1 of 2) part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response is-line\"><label for=\"y11ty-do-now-c\">(c) Write the line that makes a constant called MaxLives with the value 3 [1]</label><input id=\"y11ty-do-now-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-c\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Variables and Constants (1 of 2) part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11ty-do-now-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11ty-do-now-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "do-now-2",
   "label": "Do Now: Trace (2 of 2)",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11ty-do-now-2",
   "validatorKey": "y11ty_do_now_2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Trace (2 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does line 1 say INTEGER?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Total only ever holds whole numbers.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">From Unit 7. Trace the program.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Total : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &lt;- 10</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Count &lt;- 1 TO 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &lt;- Total - 3</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">6&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">7&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Total</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ty-do-now-2-a\">(a) What is output? [1]</label><input id=\"y11ty-do-now-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Trace (2 of 2) part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11ty-do-now-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 1 mark</strong></div><div id=\"y11ty-do-now-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "title",
   "label": "Data Types, Input and Output",
   "content": "<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">8.1 Programming Concepts</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Data Types, Input and Output</h2><p>Year 11</p></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Today:</strong> every variable has a <strong>data type</strong>: the kind of value it stores.</li><li><strong>Then:</strong> INPUT puts a typed value in a variable. OUTPUT shows it.</li></ul><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does a program need to know what kind of value it stores?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>So it knows what it can do with it. You can add two numbers, but not two names.</p></div></details>"
  },
  {
   "id": "types",
   "label": "The Five Data Types",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">The Five Data Types</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: which type is best for 3.75? For 'Y'? Why not INTEGER for both?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>3.75 is <strong>REAL</strong>: it has a decimal point. 'Y' is <strong>CHAR</strong>: one character.</p><p>INTEGER only stores whole numbers.</p></div></details><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Type</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">It stores</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Examples</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>INTEGER</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">a whole number</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">16, 25, -3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>REAL</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">a number with a decimal point</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">3.75, 1.68</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>CHAR</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">one character</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">'Y', 'A', '7'</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>STRING</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">many characters</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">\"Muhammed\", \"Room12\"</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>BOOLEAN</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE or FALSE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE</td></tr></table>"
  },
  {
   "id": "types-check",
   "label": "Check: Tick the Type",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y11ty-types-check",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Tick the Type</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is '7' a CHAR here and not an INTEGER?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It is one key from the keyboard, stored as a character. We are not doing maths with it.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/22, June 2026, Question 2 and 0478/23, June 2026, Question 2.</p><div id=\"y11ty-types-check\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "A programming data type used to store a single letter, symbol or number input from the keyboard",
     "options": [
      "Boolean",
      "char",
      "integer",
      "real"
     ],
     "correct": 1,
     "explain": "char stores one character: one letter, one symbol or one digit."
    },
    {
     "prompt": "A programming data type used to store any combination of letters and numbers",
     "options": [
      "char",
      "Boolean",
      "string",
      "real"
     ],
     "correct": 2,
     "explain": "string stores many characters, letters and numbers together."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "compare",
   "label": "Compare: Same Digits, Different Types",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Compare: Same Digits, Different Types</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Both store 16. What is different? Which one can you do maths with?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>A stores the <strong>number</strong> 16, so A + 1 is 17.</p><p>B stores the <strong>text</strong> \"16\", two characters. You cannot do maths with it.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">A: an age</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Age : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Age &lt;- 16</div></div></div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">B: a room name</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Room : STRING</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Room &lt;- \"16\"</div></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "student-table",
   "label": "Your Turn: Choose the Types",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y11ty-student-table",
   "validatorKey": "y11ty_student_table",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Your Turn: Choose the Types</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is the telephone number not an INTEGER?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It has a + and a space. We never do maths with a phone number.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/21, June 2026, Question 3. Write the best data type for each variable.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ty-student-table-a\">(a) Age: the age of the student, for example 16 [1]</label><input id=\"y11ty-student-table-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"student-table-a\" aria-label=\"Your Turn: Choose the Types part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ty-student-table-b\">(b) TelephoneNumber: for example +44 7846398573 [1]</label><input id=\"y11ty-student-table-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"student-table-b\" aria-label=\"Your Turn: Choose the Types part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y11ty-student-table-c\">(c) Teenager: whether the student is a teenager, for example TRUE [1]</label><input id=\"y11ty-student-table-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"student-table-c\" aria-label=\"Your Turn: Choose the Types part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y11ty-student-table-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y11ty-student-table-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "input-output",
   "label": "INPUT and OUTPUT",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">INPUT and OUTPUT</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: the user types Mai. What is output? Why is \"Hello \" in quotes, but Name is not?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Output: <strong>Hello Mai</strong>.</p><p>Text in quotes is shown exactly as it is. A name without quotes is a variable, so its <strong>value</strong> is shown.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Name : STRING</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Name</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Hello \", Name</div></div></div><div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>INPUT</strong> takes a value from the user and stores it in a variable.</li><li><strong>OUTPUT</strong> shows text or a value.</li><li>The lines run <strong>in order</strong>, one at a time: this is <strong>sequence</strong>.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "activity-2",
   "label": "Activity: Trace a Sequence",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "trace-table-practice",
   "embedContainerId": "y11ty-embed-2",
   "embedQuery": "view=practice&lang=cambridge&support=1",
   "embedView": "practice",
   "algorithm": {
    "title": "Lines in Sequence",
    "context": "The lines run in order, one at a time. Complete the trace table.",
